port":{"summary":["Barclays is a British bank with consumer banking, credit card and investment banking businesses. Revenue (net interest income plus noninterest income) rose 10.9% to £29.1B in 2025. Net interest income rose 12.1% to £14.5B and noninterest income rose 9.8% to £14.6B; noninterest expense rose 5.3%, and the provision for credit losses was £2.3B, versus £2.0B.","Net income to common rose 16.2% to £6.2B, or £0.42 per diluted share, and the efficiency ratio was 58.7% versus 61.8%. Barclays returned £8.4B through dividends and buybacks."],"highlights":["Revenue rose 10.9% to £29.1B.","Net interest income rose 12.1%.","Noninterest income rose 9.8% to £14.6B.","Net income to common rose 16.2% to £6.2B."],"watch":["Credit-loss provision rose 15.0% to £2.3B.","Unusual items cost £611M before tax.","Net interest income depends on interest rates.","Noninterest expense was £17.1B, up 5.3%."],"table":[["Total revenue",29.097,26.232,1],["Net interest income",14.501,12.936],["Noninterest income",14.596,13.296],["Noninterest expense",17.068,16.209],["Provision for credit losses",2.279,1.982],["Other items, net",-0.611,0.067],["Pre-tax income",9.139,8.108,1],["Income tax",1.926,1.752],["Noncontrolling interests",-0.041,-0.049],["Preferred dividends & other",-0.997,0.991],["Net income to common",6.175,5.316,1],["Diluted EPS (£)",0.423,0.348,0,"eps"],["Book value per share (£)",4.698418,4.148739,0,"eps"]],"sources":[["Barclays PLC Form 20-F filings (SEC EDGAR)","https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0000312069&type=20-F"],["Barclays financial statements (StockAnalysis)","https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/bcs/financials/"]]},"video":{"revenueLine":{"cap":"Net interest income was 50% of revenue.","say":"Net interest income made up 50 percent of revenue."},"spotlights":[{"kicker":"Revenue","big":"£29.1B","sub":"revenue · +10.9%","lines":["Net interest income £14.5B","Noninterest income £14.6B"],"cap":"Revenue rose 10.9% to £29.1B.","say":"Revenue r